Figure \ref{fig:Sensitivity_P_to_mort_kappa} shows the effect of the long-term dependence structure on the life policy's value. As $\kappa_q$ increases, the contract value decreases, which is consistent with pricing intuition. From its definition in \eqref{rq}, when $\kappa_q$ rises, the bereavement effect $r_q$ decreases. This reduction in $r_q$ implies a weaker impact of the broken heart syndrome on the surviving spouse's mortality, leading to a lower risk. Consequently, the policy price decreases to reflect this reduced risk





