\section{Mourre Estimate and Order$-1$ Ballistic Lower Bound}

Define the weight operator $Q:\CH^1(\Z^d)\to \ell^2(\Z^d)$ by 
$$(Qu)_n:=\sqrt{1+|n|^2} \, u_n,\quad n\in\Z^d.$$
%{\clo It is easy to verify that $D(Q^r)=\CH^r(\Z^d)$, $r\in\N$.}

\subsection{Spectral Projection and Weight Operator}

For a self-adjoint operator $H$ on $\ell^2(\Z^d)$, and $I\subset \R$, let
$\chi_I(H)$ be the spectral projection of $H$ corresponding to $I$.



%$H\in C^1(Q)$

%(a) His of class C1(A) if and only if the following two conditions are satisfied:
%(1) there is a constant c < ∞such that for all f ∈D(A) ∩D(H):
