	\begin{abstract}
		Solel proved that every completely contractive covariant representation of a product system $\be$ over $\mathbb N^2_0$ can be dilated to an isometric representation of $\mathbb N^2_0,$ which covers Ando's dilation result when $C^{*}$-algebra $\mathcal{M}=\mathbb{C}$ and $\mathbb{E}(\mathbf{n})=\mathbb{C},$ where $\mathbf{n}\in \mathbb N^2_0.$ That arises a natural question that exactly which type of representations dilate completely contractive covariant representation of product system $\be$ over $\mathbb N^2_0?$  To identify the isometric covariant representations for which the above has an affirmative answer is the main object of this article.
	\end{abstract}


