Let $\pi$ be a representation of $\mathcal{M}$ on a Hilbert space $\mathcal{K}.$ For $ i\in \{1, \cdots,k\},$ define an isometric covariant representation $(\rho, S^{(i)})$ of $E_i$ on the Hilbert space $\mathcal{F}(\mathbb{E})\otimes_{\pi} \mathcal{K}$ (cf. \cite{SZ08}) by  $$\rho(a):=\phi_{\infty}(a) \otimes I_{\mathcal{K}}, \:\:a \in \mathcal{M} \quad \mbox{and}\quad S^{(i)}(\xi_i)=T_{{\xi}_i} \otimes I_{\mathcal{K}},\:  \xi_i \in E_i,$$ where $T_{\xi_i}$  denotes the creation operator on $\mathcal{F}(\mathbb{E})$ determined by $\xi_i.$ We say that
